  "note": "Pin numbers of the RGE package, table 4-1, pages 10 to 13. Absolute limits, section 5.1, page 14: VCC -0.3 V to 4.1 V, any pin but VCORE -0.3 V to VCC + 0.3 V. Operating range, section 5.3, page 14: VCC 2.0 V to 3.6 V, AVCC = DVCC. VCORE needs 470 nF of 20 % or better, and the capacitance at VCC is 10 times it at the least (section 5.3, page 14): 4.7 uF. VCORE is the core's own supply and takes no load (table 4-1, note 4, page 13); section 5.18 (page 26) gives its voltage as 1.5 V typical, with no limits, and that typical value is entered for both ends. XIN and XOUT are PJ.4 and PJ.5, general-purpose digital I/O as well as the terminals of XT1 (table 4-1, page 13): they are entered as I/O between DVSS and DVCC. The QFN pad has no pin in the symbol",
